# Thumper

## Lore

A gentle, nomadic D-Bee of the Waste of Arizona: a lanky humanoid with bright yellow skin covered in dozens of twitching antennae, 2D6+12 of them on a small head with no eyes or ears, a dozen down the spine and 1D6+6 on the chest and each limb, each 6-12 inches (15-30 cm) long. Its padded flat feet make it quiet but slow, and each hand ends in three long, thin fingers.

Thumpers are blind, deaf and mute, physically and psionically, and live by other senses. They are named for the heartbeat-like thump of the telekinetic pulse they emit every few seconds, a psychic echolocation that, with their antennae, gives them a sharp picture of the world around them. Something in their make-up makes them black holes to psychic sensitives, so the Waste Ghosts and the Screamers ignore them, and those horrors keep most people away. Fewer than 20,000 are thought to live in North America, half of them in the Waste; lone wanderers and small groups, seldom more than eight, turn up across Arizona, New Mexico, northern Mexico and the lowlands of the southern Rocky Mountains.

Peaceful and friendly, they keep to themselves and live off the land as nomads, but are known to lead travellers under attack by Screamers to the edge of the Waste. Their enemies are large carnivorous predators, and humans and D-Bees who take them for monsters.

## GM Notes

The book calls the Thumper a hard character to play: talking to other races means gestures, pantomime and simply acting, which is why it says to allow the race sparingly. Size 5 feet to 5 feet 6 inches (1.5-1.7 m), weight 100-120 lbs (45-54 kg), life span 60 years, usually much shorter in its harsh habitat. As an NPC its Average Level of Experience is 1D6+4 and its R.C.C. skills use the NPC percentages, +5% per level. Value: none.

The creature row Thumper in the bestiary is the same entry for use as an NPC.
